WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.000
Minor spoilers for "Strange World" ahead.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.700
Unusual names, notable diversity, and an&nbsp;
important call to protect the planet. Here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.866
are some of the things only adults&nbsp;
noticed in Disney's "Strange World."

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.400
"Strange World," the latest theatrical&nbsp;
release from Disney's Animation Studios,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:23.160
follows Jaeger Clade, a legendary explorer&nbsp;
from Avalonia, a land that is surrounded by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:28.860
mountains on all sides. On his greatest journey to&nbsp;
finally see beyond the mountains, his son Searcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:34.380
discovers a new substance that becomes the land's&nbsp;
greatest power source. However, Jaeger doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.600
make it back from the expedition. Years later,&nbsp;
Searcher lives on a farm with his son Ethan and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.120
wife Meridian. However, it soon transpires that&nbsp;
the substance Searcher discovered years ago is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.280
dying and needs to be saved. Searcher's family&nbsp;
is swept away on an adventure that leads them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:55.800
to a strange world underneath Avalonia full&nbsp;
of alien creatures, and the missing Jaeger.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.780
"Strange World" isn't afraid to wear its genre&nbsp;
influences on its sleeve. Right from the start,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:06.480
the movie's love of pulp comics and adventure&nbsp;
stories shines in the form of visual homage. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.380
the intro to "Strange World," the credits&nbsp;
sequence begins in black-and-white before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.880
showing the cover of an old school style&nbsp;
comic featuring all the characters of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.440
Clade family. It continues in this comic&nbsp;
book style as the introduction sets up the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:22.680
prequel to the story, beginning&nbsp;
with Jaeger Clade's expedition.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:27.180
"Pulp fiction" refers to cheap, campy&nbsp;
adventure comics published in the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:32.940
half of the 20th century, up until the 1950s.&nbsp;
The movie's directors have even revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:38.160
pulp magazines are one of the main influences on&nbsp;
"Strange World." During a press day for the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.180
co-director and writer Qui Nguyen&nbsp;
revealed, via What's on Disney+,

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.380
Gabrielle Union gives an excellent performance&nbsp;
as mother, wife, and adventurer Meridian Clade in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:00.180
"Strange World." Meridian is a strong supporting&nbsp;
character, acting as a rock for both husband&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:05.640
Searcher and son Ethan, and she even gets to&nbsp;
save them from time to time. But her character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.485
and specifically her name, has a deeper&nbsp;
meaning that reinforces her role in the movie.

00:02:10.579 --> 00:02:11.738
"Brace yourself!"

00:02:11.738 --> 00:02:16.800
Meridian is not necessarily a common name, but&nbsp;
it is an intentional choice that makes sense for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.900
the character. Avid geographers will know that&nbsp;
"meridian" is an astronomical and geographical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:27.900
term used by explorers and adventurers, which&nbsp;
refers to a line of longitude. The prime meridian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:33.960
for instance, is a centerline where longitude is&nbsp;
0°. In the movie, Meridian is Searcher's center,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:38.640
as she grounds him. Additionally, while he&nbsp;
lives his life as a farmer, there is a small,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.320
reluctant part of Searcher that wants to be an&nbsp;
explorer. The fact that his wife's name is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:48.401
geographical term is seemingly another clue&nbsp;
that he subconsciously longs for adventure.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:53.040
The biggest theme that runs throughout "Strange&nbsp;
World" is the intergenerational conflict between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.320
fathers and sons. Both Jaeger and Searcher,&nbsp;
and Searcher and Ethan, have their own issues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:03.480
communicating and connecting with one another.&nbsp;
In fact, Searcher's relationship with his son is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:08.100
informed by how his father treated him, which&nbsp;
touches on the theme of generational trauma.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:12.600
However, "Strange World" also has a sense&nbsp;
of how male-centric this story might seem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:17.640
and it endeavors to prioritize its female&nbsp;
characters. Jaeger, Searcher, and Ethan find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:22.260
themselves running from some angry wildlife, and&nbsp;
they find themselves scrambling through the flora&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:27.360
and fauna. Luckily, Meridian and President Mal&nbsp;
show up just in time to rescue them from turning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.841
into alien food. In this moment, the women of&nbsp;
"Strange World" have an opportunity to shine.

00:03:32.141 --> 00:03:33.660
"Ah, is this thing dangerous?" [scream]

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:40.140
In "Strange World," Alan Tudyk voices the&nbsp;
cute and gelatinous Splat. The blue blob is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.880
one of two playful companions in the movie, the&nbsp;
other being the Clades' adorable three-legged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:49.740
pooch Legend. Disney regularly includes cute&nbsp;
and cuddly companions in its animated movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:54.180
aimed at younger audiences, and "Strange&nbsp;
World" even acknowledges and pokes fun at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.380
this practice. At one point in the movie,&nbsp;
a member of the crew notices Splat for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:03.060
first time and freaks out, getting very&nbsp;
excited. He then points to Splat and says,

00:04:03.281 --> 00:04:06.525
"So cute. I wanna merchandise it."

00:04:06.656 --> 00:04:09.480
This joke might go over the heads&nbsp;
of the film's younger audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.960
but Disney's practice of creating&nbsp;
cute characters in order to sell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:17.630
toys is well documented in everything&nbsp;
from "Strange World" to "Star Wars."

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:22.140
In "Strange World," each of the three Clade&nbsp;
men take journeys to find acceptance and peace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:26.760
with their family in a multi-layered hero's&nbsp;
journey. The movie focuses most on Ethan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.620
the youngest character and the most relatable&nbsp;
to a young, diverse audience. Ethan struggles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:36.300
with breaking out of the box that his father&nbsp;
is forcing him into and refuses to accept a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:41.640
future as a farmer. Instead, Ethan longs to be&nbsp;
an explorer like his long-lost grandfather. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:46.380
when the two finally meet at long last and get to&nbsp;
know each other, they hit it off extremely well.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:50.760
As "Strange World" continues, it becomes&nbsp;
clear that Ethan resembles his grandfather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:55.740
and naturally takes on some of his mannerisms.&nbsp;
There's even a moment on the airship during which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.820
Ethan and Jaeger stand next to one another&nbsp;
and they hold themselves in the exact same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.900
pose. With their hands on their hips, front&nbsp;
foot outward and ready to take on the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:08.520
the pose itself emphasizes the adventurer&nbsp;
spirit that the two share. It is a quick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:12.420
moment and its significance is easy&nbsp;
to miss, but this theme is reinforced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:16.200
throughout the movie as Ethan takes&nbsp;
after several other characters as well.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.520
Jaeger isn't the only family member Ethan&nbsp;
has inherited traits and mannerisms from.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.420
During "Strange World," it becomes&nbsp;
clear that Ethan's mother, Meridian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:28.560
has also inspired many of her son's&nbsp;
traits. From their need for conversation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.610
to the way they stand, Ethan and&nbsp;
Meridian share many similarities.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:37.080
Ethan's shared traits with his mother and&nbsp;
grandfather only highlight how much distance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:42.420
Ethan feels from his dad, Searcher. For instance,&nbsp;
throughout the movie, Ethan goes to everyone for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:47.520
help except for his dad. On the surface, Ethan&nbsp;
seems to be more like Jaeger and Meridian than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:53.340
his own father, and Searcher is painfully aware&nbsp;
of this fact and becomes hopelessly fixated on it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:58.181
But it's not until the final act that both father&nbsp;
and son realize what they truly have in common.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.240
"I'm not my father."

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.320
Meanwhile, Searcher's relationship with&nbsp;
his own father is challenging. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:08.220
that rocky relationship didn't get&nbsp;
any better when Jaeger abandoned him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.880
and took off without warning. It takes&nbsp;
most of the movie for them to reconcile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:16.800
but Searcher and his father eventually start&nbsp;
to set aside their differences and warm up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.240
one another. They eventually spend some time&nbsp;
hanging out together, and start to bond after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.740
the longest time apart. The difficulties they&nbsp;
face will be relatable to anyone who's ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:30.236
fallen out with a family member, or longed&nbsp;
to bond with a distant parent or relative.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:35.820
At the start of the movie, Ethan's crush stops by&nbsp;
and drops off a new card for a game called Primal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:40.380
Outpost. At first, it looks as though Primal&nbsp;
Outpost may share some similarities with Magic:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:44.460
the Gathering. But it's not Magic that&nbsp;
Primal Outpost looks most similar to when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.580
it's later played on the airship.&nbsp;
Instead, there's actually another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:52.560
popular board game that Primal Outpost seems&nbsp;
to be both paying homage to and criticizing.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.540
The setup for Primal Outpost is tile based, and&nbsp;
the objective of the game is to gain and trade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:02.700
resources. While watching the movie, it's easy to&nbsp;
see that "Strange World" is evoking Settlers of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:07.380
Catan, one of the most popular strategy board&nbsp;
games of all time. While the collectible card&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:11.220
game elements and some of the in-game rules&nbsp;
stray from what players can do in Catan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:15.240
Primal Outpost definitely feels like a&nbsp;
commentary on that game in particular.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.920
Much of this critical commentary comes&nbsp;
from Ethan. As Jaeger and Searcher argue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:24.600
about how to fight in the game, Ethan gets&nbsp;
increasingly frustrated. He suggests that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:28.320
the point of Primal Outpost is to use&nbsp;
your resources to build a better world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:33.540
which is the exact opposite of the colonialist&nbsp;
fantasy of Catan and games of its ilk.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:39.180
By the final act, it's become increasingly obvious&nbsp;
that President Mal and Searcher aren't in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.860
right. As Ethan bonds with Splat and finds awe in&nbsp;
the beauty of this new world they've discovered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:48.180
everything about the mission to save the&nbsp;
Pando plant starts to make him uneasy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:52.800
Towards the end of the movie, it's revealed to&nbsp;
Searcher and Ethan exactly how wrong they are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:55.920
solidifying one of the main themes&nbsp;
of "Strange World" in the process.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:01.380
After a classic father son fight, Ethan runs off&nbsp;
the airship and Searcher follows. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:05.100
the two discover themselves in the location&nbsp;
Jaeger was trying to reach all along,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:08.760
on the other side of the mountains. It's&nbsp;
here that they discover their planet is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:14.460
a literal living being. Sadly, the being that&nbsp;
Avalonia sits atop is dying, and specifically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:18.360
it is being killed by the Avalonians&nbsp;
harvesting the Pando plant for their energy.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:23.160
This twist turns a story that was already&nbsp;
about the environment into a full-on metaphor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:27.480
for the climate change crisis facing our&nbsp;
planet. "Strange World" literally makes its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.640
planet a living breathing creature, in order to&nbsp;
communicate the idea to its younger audience that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:37.080
the planet is alive and can be harmed. In the&nbsp;
end, "Strange World" is about learning to fix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:42.506
our mistakes but also about making sacrifices&nbsp;
in order to adjust to a new, healthier world.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:47.280
After the story wraps up, the audience is&nbsp;
transported to one year later in a flash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:52.140
forward. A voiceover from Ethan reveals what's&nbsp;
happened to Avalonia following the events of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:56.280
"Strange World." In the epilogue, Ethan talks&nbsp;
about how the last year has been incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.280 --> 00:09:00.720
difficult but that everyone has proven just&nbsp;
how resilient they are. Considering the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:04.500
that "Strange World" is being released&nbsp;
at the tail end of the COVID-19 pandemic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.740
it's hard not to think that Ethan's&nbsp;
sentiment might have a deeper meaning.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:12.180
"Strange World" is far from a throwaway&nbsp;
animation, and instead contains a crucial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:17.700
subtext about climate change that mainly adults&nbsp;
and older teens will pick up on. But beyond that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:22.980
Ethan's talk of resilience appears to reference&nbsp;
the pandemic in particular. This moment serves as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:27.180
a rallying call for all the viewers who fought&nbsp;
through a hard year, but must continue doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:31.680
the work to enact change. Ultimately, this&nbsp;
call to action is the overarching theme of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:36.577
"Strange World," with the movie asking viewers&nbsp;to care for the planet before it's too late.

